      "description": "ASAP SP1 is a carrier-neutral colocation data center in Sao Paulo, located at Av. das Nacoes Unidas, 22540. The facility is designed for enterprises, ISPs, carriers, fintechs, SaaS companies and infrastructure teams that need secure colocation with direct access to Brazil's connectivity ecosystem.\n\nThe site offers full cabinets, partial cabinets, shared rackspace, cages, suites, footprints and remote hands. ASAP SP1 has 2 MW of fully built-out power, 400 sq.m. of whitespace, 2N UPS, 2N cooling, 2N standby power, dual electrical circuits per rack and up to 7 kW per rack.\n\nFor network-driven deployments, ASAP SP1 combines colocation with ASAP Telecom's carrier background, ASN AS264144, peering ecosystem and network presence in Sao Paulo. The facility supports 24/7 onsite security, 24/7 technical staff, CCTV, biometric access control, card access control, fire suppression, MMR, loading bay, parking and operational amenities for technical teams.\n\nBest fit: critical infrastructure colocation, ISP and carrier presence in Sao Paulo, enterprise server hosting, hybrid cloud edge, disaster recovery and low-latency connectivity projects.",
